================================================================================
Data Sources
================================================================================

BIC/SWIFT data, including registered/head-office addresses, is sourced from
GLEIF (Global Legal Entity Identifier Foundation) reference data under
CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication:
  https://www.gleif.org/en/about/open-data

The BIC-to-LEI mapping used to key this data to BIC codes is published by GLEIF
in collaboration with SWIFT and is provided under SWIFT's royalty-free,
commercial-use terms, which require the following attribution:
  "This service uses the BIC to LEI relationship file. The mapping table has
   been developed by SWIFT. SWIFT and BIC are registered trademarks of S.W.I.F.T. SC."
  https://www.gleif.org/en/lei-data/lei-mapping/download-bic-to-lei-relationship-files

Swiss BC-Nummer / clearing data is sourced from SIX Group AG BankMaster:
  https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/payment-services/bc-bank-master.html

Bank-level (BIC8) sanctions indicators are built directly from the official,
freely-redistributable consolidated sanctions lists published by:
  - OFAC (U.S. Office of Foreign Assets Control) — SDN list, U.S. public domain
  - European Union — consolidated financial sanctions list
This file attributes data sources, so it lists only feeds that actually put
rows in the database: OFAC accounts for all but one of them. No third-party
aggregator is used, so there is no non-commercial (CC-BY-NC) data dependency.

Country risk indicators are derived from publicly available FATF
(Financial Action Task Force) statements and the sanctions lists above.
